# Independent review of graph/3.8.kg (the round-two study of the folder nums-go-2023). One review node per claim, each naming the digest it read. Every cited local file was opened at the cited lines; the miniature was copied to a scratch directory and run again under Python 3.15.0 with the reviewer's own probe; git read commands were run in Coherence-Network, NUMS.Go, Living-Codex-CSharp, one further checkout and the old body. NUMS.Go was not built again: its run is read from the study's three stored outputs. The old runtime was not run. No web request was made (the file has no relayed claim).

n: 9.5.13
kind: hub
name: review-of-nums-study-2026
is: All 39 claims of 3.8.kg (25 observations, 14 findings) were read against their sources: 32 confirmed, 7 amended (3.8.1.6, 3.8.2.5, 3.8.3.3, 3.8.8.4, 3.8.8.6, 3.8.9.1, 3.8.9.4), none disputed, none left unreviewed. The amendments: the miniature prints 14 assertions, not 15; the quoted Living Codex lines are of 2025-10-07 at lines 572-575, not of 2025-09-12; the body re-read the kind-to-state mapping as a resting tendency and did not withdraw it; three statements claim more than their premises or contradict sibling nodes.
limit: Hubs and source nodes are outside the review, and three of them repeat an amended fact: hubs 3.8 and 3.8.2 and source 2.16.7 say 15 assertions; source 2.16.21 gives rev 6ea184a, date 2025-09-12 and lines 571-574 for a passage that is at lines 572-575 of the 869-line head and entered the file on 2025-10-07; source 2.16.1 says 463 lines where wc -l counts 462.
